From: vv-manet <willjvest@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wireless: start a vif's network ifindex at -1, not 0

wireless_check_interface() reports a network's device ifindex only when that
device has hotplug ops (a bridge). For any other network, such as a
batman-adv hard interface on a bare mesh vif, the live check returns -1. But a
new vif's stored value comes from calloc and is 0. So the first
wdev_check_network_enabled() after the radio comes up sees a change, sets
config_update, and reloads the whole radio once per boot. Morse radios set
reconf 0, so that reload is a full down/up: ~5.6 s, plus a second mesh
start scan, on the Heltec HT-HD01 with OpenMANET 1.8.0.

Start both the vif's and the vlan's stored ifindex at -1, the value the check
uses for "no bridge", so the two agree from the first check.

Came in with 3c6265f ("reload wireless device if any vif network bridge
changes ifindex").
---
--- a/wireless.c	2026-10-23 22:16:20.932602950 -0400
+++ b/wireless.c	2026-10-23 22:16:20.990638205 -0400
@@ -1209,6 +1209,7 @@
 	sprintf(name, "%d", vif->vlan_idx++);
 
 	vlan = calloc_a(sizeof(*vlan), &name_buf, strlen(name) + 1);
+	vlan->network_ifindex = -1;
 	vlan->name = strcpy(name_buf, name);
 	vlan->config = data;
 	vlan->section = section;
@@ -1252,6 +1253,7 @@
 		       &name_buf, strlen(name) + 1);
 	vif->name = strcpy(name_buf, name);
 	vif->wdev = wdev;
+	vif->network_ifindex = -1;
 	vif->config = data;
 	vif->section = section;
 	vif->isolate = false;
